{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024334-travelling-mages","id":1024334,"title":"Travelling Mages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-30T08:07:16-08:00","id":1024334,"title":"Travelling Mages","content":"I am going to try my hand at Storytelling a Mage the Awakening 2e game on a PbP sight (Myth-weavers). The members of the cabal are a rock band and on tour they travel from city to city. How should the local <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Consilium view such travelling mages and should there be a Consilium in every city. And is it possible and a good idea to make the tour bus a Sanctum?<br /> <br /> The base idea is that the music is their magic sort of thing.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T08:12:46-08:00","id":1024340,"title":"","content":"How a Consilium reacts depends on their reputation and level of respect for the local laws. Not every city has a Consilium, those only crop up around Mysteries, and yeah a tour bus can be a Sanctum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T08:16:51-08:00","id":1024344,"title":"","content":"Consilia are mostly a Diamond thing. Cities where the Free Council is the majority will have an Assembly that Diamond mages participate in as part of their alliance as the Pentacle. Cities where the Seers of the Throne dominate will be managed by a large-scale pylon answering to the dominant Ministry. (Pylons are the Seer equivalents to cabals and columns, but pylons are typically larger due to Seers being obsessed with hierarchy and a chain of command) And then there are cities with no particular mage government, due to having no special mystery to chase and thus having a low mage population.<br /> <br /> Whether a city will welcome them depends on which sect your rock band belong to, and the current political climate and/or past history the city has had with outsiders.<br /> <br /> Don't recall the Sanctum rules right now, so can't comment on that.<br /> <br /> Great idea on magic music, though. They can use it as Yantras, Shadow Names, the Cabal Theme, a way to cover up overt magic and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T08:29:12-08:00","id":1024353,"title":"","content":"Mages you don't know are all possible enemies. Unless the characters arrive with a letter of introduction from a Hierarch or similarly potent figure that the receiving Consilium is familiar with and trusts, expect a frosty reception at best. Moreover, expect other Mages feeling very uncharitable when they spot the newcomers in their territory.<br /> <br /> Of course, this assumes the characters care to be spotted. They might arrive, perform, and leave without stirring the pot. As long as other Mages aren't in the area at the time when they cast a spell, they'll be fine. It's entirely possible that Mages wander through the cities of other Awakened all the time and never know about each others' presence.<br /> <br /> The trouble comes when a Mystery presents itself and they can't help but give chase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T08:30:07-08:00","id":1024354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024334-travelling-mages?p=1024344#post1024344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great idea on magic music, though. They can use it as Yantras, Shadow Names, the Cabal Theme, a way to cover up overt magic and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was my thought on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T08:40:04-08:00","id":1024358,"title":"","content":"Having connections with the Mysterium Egregore is a good way to get your bona fides when traveling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T10:20:07-08:00","id":1024389,"title":"","content":"Order Status would help, compared to Consilium Status.<br /> <br /> You would definitely want a sanctum traveling with them, unless you're going the 'PCs automatically regen mana during downtime' route.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T10:29:51-08:00","id":1024391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024334-travelling-mages?p=1024389#post1024389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Order Status would help, compared to Consilium Status.<br /> <br /> You would definitely want a sanctum traveling with them, unless you're going the 'PCs automatically regen mana during downtime' route.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ya, I won't be forcing them to take anything in particular but it will be suggested that they take certain stuff.<br /> <br /> I have also described their Manager as odd, he is the one that books their tour and they seem to arrive in town at the worst of times as thing in the supernatural world are in upheaval, or thing in the sleeper world are bad, or a little of both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T10:33:45-08:00","id":1024395,"title":"","content":"This is part of the introduction and i feel it is accurate.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Music has captivated the young and old alike. Music can sooth the raging heart, or inflame the masses. It can bring sorrow or joy. Lovers choose a song that will remind them of their love. Nothing can stir human emotions quit like music as it can speak to the very sole. Music is magical and in your case literally&quot;</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T10:52:32-08:00","id":1024404,"title":"","content":"Is not in 2E <b>Mage</b> corebook music inspired chronicle cast creation tool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T11:06:49-08:00","id":1024410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024334-travelling-mages?p=1024404#post1024404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is not in 2E <b>Mage</b> corebook music inspired chronicle cast creation tool?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nor sure what this is supposed to mean? No music itself isn't magical but the median that they use to cast their magic is music. The lyrics and musical notes can be Yantras, instruments can be dedicated magic tools.<br /> <br /> Haven't you ever listened to a song that was so sad that you welled up and almost cried, that is mind control affecting your emotions. Concentrated sound can break bones, forces effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T11:08:03-08:00","id":1024411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024334-travelling-mages?p=1024389#post1024389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Order Status would help, compared to Consilium Status.<br /> <br /> You would definitely want a sanctum traveling with them, unless you're going the 'PCs automatically regen mana during downtime' route.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what way do you think that a Sanctum eases mana usage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T11:11:21-08:00","id":1024412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024334-travelling-mages?p=1024391#post1024391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have also described their Manager as odd, he is the one that books their tour and they seem to arrive in town at the worst of times as thing in the supernatural world are in upheaval, or thing in the sleeper world are bad, or a little of both.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has me thinking the underlying Mystery of the Chronicle is the tour itself. I think I'd want to play a Mage who has barely any musical talent at all but is faking it in order to get in the band and get in on this rockin' Mystery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T11:18:21-08:00","id":1024415,"title":"","content":"I can't say much here as I know atleast one of the potential group does visit this forum I believe 3 of them are but not sure. But the Manager is involved.<br /> <br /> P.S. I told them that they didn't actually need to be one of the band members that they could be any of the support staff up to but excluding the manager.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T13:33:52-08:00","id":1024483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024334-travelling-mages?p=1024411#post1024411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In what way do you think that a Sanctum eases mana usage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pardon, I meant Hallow. It's a location that produces Mana, in Merit form similar to Sanctum. Sorry to have confused you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T13:56:06-08:00","id":1024488,"title":"","content":"Hallows don't move so it wouldn't do a traveling rock band any good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T14:13:47-08:00","id":1024493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024334-travelling-mages?p=1024410#post1024410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nor sure what this is supposed to mean? No music itself isn't magical but the median that they use to cast their magic is music. The lyrics and musical notes can be Yantras, instruments can be dedicated magic tools.<br /> <br /> Haven't you ever listened to a song that was so sad that you welled up and almost cried, that is mind control affecting your emotions. Concentrated sound can break bones, forces effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct on the Yantras usage and all. I just pointed that in 2E corebook is music based tool for chronicle creation, maybe adding next depth to the game - on normal purpose I would not use it, but mata-narrating rock band by creating stories plot on interwining rock songs for the group of rockers could work golden for this type of game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T14:18:09-08:00","id":1024495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024334-travelling-mages?p=1024488#post1024488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hallows don't move so it wouldn't do a traveling rock band any good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that shared Legacy based on music would solve any Mana problems - <i>any</i> Legacy for the groups members, for that matter. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thinking on Legacy based on music itself, I think that Silver Ladder and Free Council groups are most appropiate candidates. Did not 1E Skalds were all about it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T14:36:39-08:00","id":1024502,"title":"","content":"Yeah, legacies and sacrifices would pretty much cover any man's needs.<br /> <br /> A Hallow could work if there was a means of Sympathetically accessing it either via a Mage with Space and Prime or an item.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T14:38:45-08:00","id":1024504,"title":"","content":"It's time for another Magical Mystery Tour! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In addition to the Shadow Name and Cabal Theme Merits, consider taking Fame (and maintain a good magical reputation) as a means to ease relations (and weaken Sympathy) as the band travels through different territories.<br /> <br /> Damn, now I want to play a 1970's Mage chronicle with a cabal based on Kiss. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T14:47:19-08:00","id":1024507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024334-travelling-mages?p=1024504#post1024504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn, now I want to play a 1970's Mage chronicle with a cabal based on Kiss. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And everyone gets a little bit nervous around the blood spitting Mage with &quot;the Demon&quot; as his Shadow Name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":".  Forgot Gene Simmons' stage name. 12-30-2016, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T14:56:54-08:00","id":1024512,"title":"","content":"I think it going to be a great game, I was think the almost must have for the merits would be Cabal Theme, Shadow Name, Sanctum. I was seriously thinking of making the bus an artifact but a Sanctum would do. One of the things I was thinking is that the cities are already in distress both magically and mundane. Music sooths the savage beast and eventually the city calms down, so they have a rep of making things better in the places that they play in. This could smooth the way for to visit. Now rock bands are not known for being to peaceful themselves but somehow whatever they did fixed it.<br /> <br /> Now without saying to much as who knows who will read this. The Manager is involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T15:08:40-08:00","id":1024513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024334-travelling-mages?p=1024507#post1024507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And everyone gets a little bit nervous around the blood spitting Mage with &quot;the Beast&quot; as his Shadow Name.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Great and now I can envision that, Thanks. LOL I just hope that they do not choose disco as their sound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T17:14:06-08:00","id":1024573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024334-travelling-mages?p=1024507#post1024507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And everyone gets a little bit nervous around the blood spitting Mage with &quot;the Demon&quot; as his Shadow Name.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Gene Simmons: Seer or Libertine? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-sHMAY-AqhM\" data-code=\"-sHMAY-AqhM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/-sHMAY-AqhM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 12-30-2016, 08:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T02:02:21-08:00","id":1024673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024334-travelling-mages?p=1024488#post1024488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hallows don't move so it wouldn't do a traveling rock band any good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could totally see a Prime spell that nests a Hallow in a van.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T02:39:52-08:00","id":1024687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024334-travelling-mages?p=1024673#post1024673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could totally see a Prime spell that nests a Hallow in a van.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It would be like a cell phone connecting to the various different cell towers as it travels, except that it would connect to various other hollows/lay lines that it passes and get some Mana from each.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T02:50:53-08:00","id":1024689,"title":"","content":"Or a Space spell. Maybe a Co-location variant with the following: Add Prime 2: Target a number of locations equal to Potency; one location containing a Hallow. This spell superimposes the flow of the Hallow with the other locations. Tass produced by this Hallow will coalesce evenly in every location targeted by the spell but the total amount of Tass in all locations determines when the Hallow is considered filled to capacity. Mages may perform Oblations at these locations as if they were inside the Hallow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T07:16:23-08:00","id":1024749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024334-travelling-mages?p=1024687#post1024687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be like a cell phone connecting to the various different cell towers as it travels, except that it would connect to various other hollows/lay lines that it passes and get some Mana from each.</div> </div> </div> </div>There aren't a lot of unclaimed Hallows so while this is a cool idea it'd be seen as poaching and wouldn't make you any friends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T07:49:16-08:00","id":1024757,"title":"","content":"If travelling with Hallow nested in a storage isn't cool... maybe a Matter 4/Prime 4 artefact that gathers road dust into tass? The more you travel the more you have of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 12-31-2016, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T09:00:23-08:00","id":1024776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024334-travelling-mages?p=1024757#post1024757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If travelling with Hallow nested in a storage isn't cool... maybe a Matter 4/Prime 4 artefact that gathers road dust into tass? The more you travel the more you have of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or something similar where they can gather tass by travelling on roads that coincides with ley lines. That would make for interesting tour patterns that might attract attention if they're famous enough (if they're also a band), or simply lead up to ley line related mysteries in a very natural manner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T09:27:35-08:00","id":1024786,"title":"","content":"If a player invests in the Artifact Merit for their character, that's a mobile regenerating mana pool right there, though obviously not on the level of a proper Hallow.<br /> <br /> The Mysterium book in 1E had a merit for a mobile sanctum (though that was more for backpacking Indiana Jones-types), so a tour bus could absolutely work!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T09:29:59-08:00","id":1024787,"title":"","content":"Artifacts no longer generate mana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T09:36:41-08:00","id":1024790,"title":"","content":"They store mana and if it had prime 3 it could collect it. But I think the bestway would be to have an spacial/prime effect that could link the bus to a hollow that they have rightful access to. Also they would have an easier chance if they belong to a Legacy and used their Oblations. I wish I know of a good legacy for them that would use their music as an Oblations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T17:17:40-08:00","id":1024948,"title":"","content":"If you want music to work as an Oblation then just house rule it, don't hesitate if it works with your chronicle.<br /> If you really want their tour bus to work like a mobile hallow then again just house rule it, give it an interesting background and declare it a mystery.<br /> \u200bIf all you need is a way to gather Mana you could give them an item that collects the Essence generated by their audiences and converts it to Mana. Perhaps a ridiculous statue that appears in all of their cover art.<br /> \u200bDon't neglect roadies and crew, Sleepwalkers can hold 'Sanctum' spells in place of a Hallow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T17:19:48-08:00","id":1024949,"title":"","content":"There's at least two music related legacies the Skalds and I forget the name of the other one I think it's in the Mysterium book. Technically the Pygmalians also count if music is the medium of art of their choice. There's probably more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T18:01:33-08:00","id":1024959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024334-travelling-mages?p=1024948#post1024948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want music to work as an Oblation then just house rule it, don't hesitate if it works with your chronicle.<br /> If you really want their tour bus to work like a mobile hallow then again just house rule it, give it an interesting background and declare it a mystery.<br /> \u200bIf all you need is a way to gather Mana you could give them an item that collects the Essence generated by their audiences and converts it to Mana. Perhaps a ridiculous statue that appears in all of their cover art.<br /> \u200bDon't neglect roadies and crew, Sleepwalkers can hold 'Sanctum' spells in place of a Hallow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I could just house rule it, however I like looking for the way to do it. Their are alot of ways to do alot of things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024334-travelling-mages?p=1024949#post1024949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's at least two music related legacies the Skalds and I forget the name of the other one I think it's in the Mysterium book. Technically the Pygmalians also count if music is the medium of art of their choice. There's probably more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will look at those legacies, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T18:40:46-08:00","id":1024967,"title":"","content":"Singers in Silence is the one I couldn't think of. Tamers of Fire and Bearers of the Eternal Voice aren't specifically musical but they both work well with music in their way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T01:38:47-08:00","id":1025032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024334-travelling-mages?p=1024967#post1024967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Singers in Silence is the one I couldn't think of. Tamers of Fire and Bearers of the Eternal Voice aren't specifically musical but they both work well with music in their way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Of the 3 of them The Skalds are the closest and I will need to convert them to 2e before they are ready. The next closest is the Pygmalians and then the Singers in Silence.<br /> <br /> My question is<br /> #1) Should they all share a Legacy and if so then they would all need to take the Arcanum (Mind for the emotion control or possibly Fate, Optional based in spirit).<br /> #2) Are there subsets to Legacies that exist within a Legacy. Example you are not just a cop you are an internal affairs cop.<br /> #3) If a cabal was made up of members of different legacies that were thematically closely tied together, would they actually start to meld beliefs and form such a, 1 off, subset of the legacies involved. Example: A Skuld, Singer in Silence, and a Pygmalian (walk into this bar, <i>no bad joke</i>) Their themes are somewhat close to each other would there different approach to a common theme start to morph their overall beliefs into a subset of all three? I can see this bringing them closer together or driving them apart like so many bands end up doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 01-01-2017, 04:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T02:03:31-08:00","id":1025033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024334-travelling-mages?p=1025032#post1025032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of the 3 of them The Skalds are the closest and I will need to convert them to 2e before they are ready. The next closest is the Pygmalians and then the Singers in Silence.</div> </div> </div> </div>With Skalds I may help you on update to 2E - I was wanting to add them to my games. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> With changes to 2E format I would be seeing them as Acanthus Legacy, with Primary Mind and secondary Fate. Twist is they would be Silver Ladder <b>and</b> Free Council ones, as Skalds would greatly work in creation of Council of Free Assemblies ( and generally as Messengers in Libertines ) or to sustaining Sleepers traditions based Technes ( like literal Skalds of Scandianvia or other similar roles in other cultures ).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024334-travelling-mages?p=1025032#post1025032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">#1) Should they all share a Legacy and if so then they would all need to take the Arcanum (Mind for the emotion control and possibly Fate).</div> </div> </div> </div>In reality, your PCs just need a Legacy, not the Legacy. ANY Legacy will generate enough Mana, as almost all Oblations are rather simple to fulfill. You must remember that having teacher is only one of ways you can be student in Legacy - you can just have get proper Grimoire ( Daimonomicon ) or get hands over Soul Stone of Legacy member. Many possibilities here.<br /> <br /> But shearing one thematic Legacy will ease game and let stories to flourish on this Legacies themes. Still, you can simple have mix of many Awakened musicians, it's just the best would be if they have Legacy.<br /> <br /> If you make 2E Skalds as I advise ( Mind Primary, Fate Secondary ) they all would need to have dots in Mind to have Attainments at all. BUT there is common house rule that if you have Legacies Primary Arcanum as Ruling, you can take Secondary as third one. It's almost so common it's universal rule in most 2E chronicles. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> With this rule, Mastigos joining Skalds would get Fate as third Ruling Arcanum at his disposal.<br /> <br /> Finally, remember that Legacy members can be outside Legacies Parent Path or Order(s) - he just will have a bit harder learning time, as he will need make each Legacy Attainment from his own Praxis. Even if Skalds would be Acanthus, Silver Ladder and Free Council - you <i>totally</i> <i>could</i> have members like Mysterium Thyrsus or Arrow Moros. They just will need to take 'harder road'. ( That in the end is even more XP positive for them, from Praxis-to-Attainments refund <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024334-travelling-mages?p=1025032#post1025032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">#2) Are there subsets to Legacies that exist within a Legacy. Example you are not just a cop you are an internal affairs cop.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, many Legacies have factions inside them, with slightly changed Attainments. On official ones, <i>Bene Ashmedai</i> and <i>Clavicularius</i> were having common origin group, but separated in to two proper Legacies over ideological differences.<br /> <br /> Remember also that Legacies Attainments are default ones - you character can make his own variants if he wants - it only is a bit more costly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024334-travelling-mages?p=1025032#post1025032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">#3) If a cabal was made up of members of different legacies that were thematically closely tied together, would they actually start to meld beliefs and form such a 1 off subset of the legacies involved. Example: A Skuld, Singer in Silence, and a Pygmalian (walk into this bar, <i>no bad joke</i>) Their themes are somewhat close to each other would there different approach to a common theme start to morph their overall beliefs?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand a question here - Legacies, in reality, are collection of Attainments, Yantras, Oblations and few other minor tricks. You can totally change Attainments, but others are rather set in stone as you chose Legacy. What mages do with their Legacy is their own business, only that they are marked on one forever on. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-01-2017, 05:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T02:26:05-08:00","id":1025037,"title":"","content":"Good maybe we can collaborate on a 2e version of the Skalds (of course everyone that wanted to could also collaborate). I forgot that each member could create there own Attainments from Praxis that they know.<br /> <br /> Basically what I was asking, in question #3, is if 3 people of different legacies were to be together for a while and find that their individual legacies are similar, would they in essence start to form their own legacy, reshaping their souls into something different?<br /> <br /> BTW I was also looking at the side bar, Legacies of the Ancient page 87, of the Skalds that mention a possible smaller and less well know legacy that could be similar to the Skalds. Their members might be called The Orpheans","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 01-01-2017, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T02:52:28-08:00","id":1025040,"title":"","content":"I will reread today, maybe tomorrow Skalds and post my ideas on update in separate topic. As to merging of Legacies - most important part is that Legacies are Path-based ( Orders are added on 'higher layer' over this ). If all cabal members would be from one Path, and everyone agree they could change their Attainments on semi-consistent way - they, technically, <i>will </i>creating their own Legacy. But it still would be not 'proper' Legacy till they would not have students on it, second generation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T03:10:07-08:00","id":1025041,"title":"","content":"I will make a post for the Skalds and put a template in it to start working from. The template will ne mostly blank to be filled in as the development continues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T10:07:25-08:00","id":1025097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024334-travelling-mages?p=1025032#post1025032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question is<br /> #1) Should they all share a Legacy and if so then they would all need to take the Arcanum (Mind for the emotion control or possibly Fate, Optional based in spirit).<br /> #2) Are there subsets to Legacies that exist within a Legacy. Example you are not just a cop you are an internal affairs cop.<br /> #3) If a cabal was made up of members of different legacies that were thematically closely tied together, would they actually start to meld beliefs and form such a, 1 off, subset of the legacies involved. Example: A Skuld, Singer in Silence, and a Pygmalian (walk into this bar, <i>no bad joke</i>) Their themes are somewhat close to each other would there different approach to a common theme start to morph their overall beliefs into a subset of all three? I can see this bringing them closer together or driving them apart like so many bands end up doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>1: I wouldn't make them, that kind of thing is for the players to decide, on top of that you're not forcing the players to play actual members of the band. A roadie might be more interested in being a Master of the Inanimate just for instance.<br /> <br /> 2: If there are it's usually just an organizational thing rather than developing different attainments from each other. Developing different attainments leads to being in actually different legacies, hence why the Clavicularius and the Bene Ashemedai don't act like a single group.<br /> <br /> 3: Members of different legacies will effect the outlooks of each other to the extent that socializing with someone who has a different life experience than you will effect you. It won't lead to any kind of melding of their legacy attainments or anything though. Yes though their similarities or differences can causes bonds of breaks inside of the group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}